=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_3f7c — The laptop migration: coffee table overnight, desk 10–17, coffee table evening (fork of p_a1b2)

Two young adults share a flat. Marco (late twenties) works in a downtown office, leaving around 08:00 and returning around 17:30 on weekdays. Omar (late twenties) works from home, but his laptop does NOT sit at desk_o1 all day. The evidence over three days shows a clear migration: overnight and in the early morning (03:00–09:00) the laptop rests at coffee_table_l1 (sometimes bookshelf_l1); by 10:00 it is at desk_o1 for the core work block; it stays at desk_o1 through 13:00 and 15:00; and by 18:00 it is back at coffee_table_l1 for the evening. Omar's "work hours" at the desk are roughly 10:00–17:00, not 09:00–17:30.

What changed from p_a1b2 and why: the claim "Omar's laptop is at desk_o1 during weekday work hours 9–17.5" scored 4-for / 15-against. The 09:00 sightings show the laptop at coffee_table_l1 (2×) or bookshelf_l1 (1×), not at the desk. The 18:00 sighting shows it back at coffee_table_l1. I have moved the desk block to 10:00–17:00 and added coffee_table_l1 blocks for 0–10 and 17–22. The rest of the household routine (Marco's commute, weekend errands, shared evening) is unchanged.

What would refute this fork: laptop_omar sighted at desk_o1 at 09:00 on a weekday (implying an earlier start than the data supports); or laptop_omar sighted at desk_o1 at 18:00 or later on a weekday (implying he works past 17:00).

