# p_9d2e — The 19:00 cook: pan on counter at 19:00, snack bowl on counter, remote stays at TV (fork of p_789a)

This household runs on a tight evening schedule, but the cooking window is later than p_789a assumed. The robot's passes show the pan in the cupboard at 18:00 and on the counter at 19:00 (2×), back in the cupboard at 20:00. The kitchen knife follows the same arc: drawer at 18:00, counter at 19:00. So the active cooking window is approximately 18:30–19:30, not 17:30–19:00. Dinner (plates at the kitchen table) happens at 19:00–19:30.

What changed from p_789a and why: (1) The pan block moved from 17.5–19 to 18.5–19.5; the 17.5–19 window scored 0-for / 12-against. (2) The snack bowl is on the kitchen COUNTER (counter_k1) during the evening, not on the coffee table. Sightings at 18:00 show it at counter_k1 (2×) and at 20:00 at counter_k1 (3×); it has never been seen at coffee_table_l1. The "snack bowl on coffee table" claim scored 0-for / 7-against. (3) The remote stays on the TV stand (tv_stand_l1) even during the TV block. It has never been sighted at coffee_table_l1 in any pass. The "remote on coffee table" claim scored 0-for / 3-against. (4) Plates are at the kitchen table 19:00–19:5 (sightings show 4× at kitchen_table at 19:00).

What sets this apart from p_789a: the cooking is later (18:30–19:30), the snack bowl lives on the counter (Omar's snacking station), and the remote never leaves the TV stand. The "cooking together, TV together, no solo hobbies" narrative is preserved.

What would refute it: pan sighted on the counter at 18:00 (cooking started earlier than the data supports); snack bowl sighted at coffee_table_l1 at any hour; remote sighted at coffee_table_l1.

